            "url": "https://www.npr.org/2019/05/29/727850485/plenty-of-cards-to-play-chinese-media-suggest-cutting-rare-earth-exports-to-u-s",
            "title": "'Plenty Of Cards To Play': Chinese Media Suggest Cutting Rare Earth ...",
            "snippets": [
              "- Keyboard shortcuts for audio player\n\n**'Plenty Of Cards To Play': Chinese Media Suggest Cutting Rare Earth Exports To U.S.** **Rare earths are used in communications, health care and national security. China blocked rare earths to Japan in 2010, but analysts say the threat — regardless of the trade war — may be hollow.**",
              "# 'Plenty Of Cards To Play': Chinese Media Suggest Cutting Rare Earth Exports To U.S.\n### World\n\nMay 29, 2019 2:08 PM ET\n\nBy\n\nSasha Ingber\n\nEnlarge this image\n\nA worker in China shifts soil containing rare earth minerals intended for export in 2010. Rare earths are used in important technologies, and a commentary in China's People's Daily newspaper on Wednesday said the U.S. endangers its supply from China by waging a trade war. **STR/AFP/Getty Images** ****hide caption****",
